# TEMPLATE, NOT DEPLOYABLE. auth_method, event_outcome and vpn_user are placeholders.
# No documented SonicOS log field records the SSL-VPN authentication method. Kept out of CI
# by the .template suffix. Do not deploy until you have validated a field on your own firewall.
title: SonicWall SSL-VPN Login Without SAML For SAML-Enforced User (CVE-2026-19868)
id: 7d3b9e42-5c1a-4f6e-8a20-3b9c1d7e4f53
status: unsupported
description: |
  Detects successful SonicOS SSL-VPN logins recorded with a non-SAML
  authentication method. CVE-2026-19868 lets valid credentials for an
  alternate method bypass SAML and SAML-enforced MFA when SAML is enabled for
  SSL-VPN. Field names are placeholders: map auth_method, event_outcome and
  vpn_user to your SonicOS syslog parser, and scope to users who should only
  use SAML.
references:
  - https://psirt.global.sonicwall.com/vuln-detail/SNWLID-2026-0014
  - https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2026/11/06/cisa-adds-one-known-exploited-vulnerability-catalog
  - https://github.com/CyberThreatNet/hunt-lab/tree/main/hunts/2026/2026-11-07-sonicwall-sslvpn-saml-bypass
author: Cyber-Threat.net Hunt Lab
date: 2026-11-07
tags:
  - attack.initial-access
  - attack.t1133
  - attack.persistence
  - attack.t1078
  - attack.credential-access
  - attack.t1556
  - cve.2026-19868
  - detection.emerging-threats
logsource:
  product: sonicwall
  service: sslvpn
detection:
  selection:
    event_outcome: success
  saml:
    auth_method|contains: saml
  condition: selection and not saml
fields:
  - vpn_user
  - auth_method
  - src_ip
  - event_outcome
falsepositives:
  - Documented break-glass local accounts
  - Users legitimately allowed to use non-SAML methods
level: high
